<Post route="/blog/large-deposit-letter" page="post2" n="02" title="What the large deposit rule asks for, and what a drafted letter should say" standfirst="The two thresholds, where a source has to come from, how seasoning is read across two statements, and the six things the borrower's letter has to carry." tag="deposits" ph="PH-07" phAlt="Two bank statement pages side by side on a desk, one line under the lamp." scene="threshold" poster="W-07" posterAlt="A still of the post 2 threshold plane scene: two columns of deposit figures with the translucent threshold plane resting across them, the figures above it lit." sceneText="the threshold plane: 4,206.25 conventional and 4,120.00 FHA sliding down two columns of deposits" footerIndex="0004" button={{ label: 'Buy a file pack', price: 'from $2,400', href: '/pricing#ledger' }} link={{ label: 'Or order the Pilot at $0', href: '/cart?pilot=1', pilot: true }}>
